-destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
(Note: destination_availability_locked unchanged)

S7.

Step8: detach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: true (still)
Effects:
+route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha
-candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha

S8.

Step9: attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_created origin_availability_alpha: true
- vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha: true (init true, unchanged)
- route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha: true (just made true by detach)
Effects:
+candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
-route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha

S9.

Step10: confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_created origin_availability_alpha: true
- vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha: true
- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: true
- not candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: true (init false, we haven't prepared origin yet)
Effects:
+candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha

S10.

Step11: activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: true
- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: true
- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha: true
- not origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha: true (init false)
- not origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha: true (init false)
Effects:
+origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha

S11.

Step12: load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: true
- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha: true
- cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha: true (we got cargo back from step7)
- not origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha: true (init false, not yet locked)
Effects:
+origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha
+origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha
+origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
-cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha

S12.

Step13: unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha.

Preconditions:
- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: true
- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: true
- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha: true
- origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha: true (from step12)
- origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha: true (from step12)
- not origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha: true (init false)
Effects:
+origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (still true)
+origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha
+cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha
-origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
(origin_availability_locked unchanged)

S13.

Step14: assemble_transport_leg origin_availability_alpha destination_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha destination_node_alpha transport_leg_alpha.

Preconditions:
- origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha: true (from step12)
- destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha: true (from step6)
- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha: true
- destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha: true
- origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha: true (from step11, still true after step13)
- destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha: true (from step5, still true after step7)
- origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha: true (from step13)
- destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha: true (from step7)
- transport_leg_available transport_leg_alpha: true (init true, not used yet)
Effects:
+transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha
+transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha
+transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha
-transport_leg_available transport_leg_alpha

S14.

Step15: execute_schedule_dispatch shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma dispatch_slot_alpha.

Preconditions:
- dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha: true (init true)
- candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma: true (init true)
- candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha: true (init true)
- not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha: true (init false)
Effects:
+dispatched shift_candidate_alpha
+vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma
+dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha

S15 (final).

Now verify goal predicates in final state S15:

- candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha: true (S3)
- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha: true (S10)
- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha: true (S9, not detached)
- candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta: true (S1)
- destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha: true (S7)
- destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha: true (S6, still true)
- destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha: true (S6)
- destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha: true (S5, still true after S7)
- dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha: true (S15)
- dispatched shift_candidate_alpha: true (S15)
- origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha: true (S13)
- origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha: true (S12)
- origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha: true (S12)
- origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha: true (S11, still true after S13)
- transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha: true (S14)
- transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha: true (S14)
- transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha: true (S14)
- vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha: true (S1)
- vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma: true (S15)

All satisfied.

Thus plan is valid.

Now we need to ensure minimal number of actions. Could we reduce any steps? Perhaps we could skip detach_task_profile if we keep task profile linked to destination and also attach to origin? Not possible due to availability constraint. Could we avoid assigning operator to destination? Goal does not require operator link for destination. However lock action not needed because we got confirmed via unload. But we still needed operator for lock? Actually we didn't use lock at all; we used load/unload to get confirmed and locked. So we didn't need operator for destination. However we used assign_operator_resource for destination; maybe we can skip it because we never used lock. Let's see: we used load and unload; load required not destination_availability_locked (we had false before load). After load we got locked true. Unload required not destination_availability_confirmed (we had false). After unload we got confirmed true, lock remained true. So we never needed operator. So assign_operator_resource is unnecessary. Good catch! So we can remove step4.

Similarly for origin we didn't need operator either; we didn't use lock. So we can skip assign_operator for both.

Thus we can remove assign_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha.

Now we need to check if any other action requires operator. No.

Thus we can eliminate that action.

Now check if any other action requires operator availability later? No.

Thus we reduce plan by one action.

Now we also might consider if we need to allocate vehicle for origin? It's already allocated; we skip.

Now we need to verify that we didn't inadvertently need operator for something else like confirm_candidate_preparedness? No.

Thus revised plan steps:

1 allocate_vehicle_unit destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta
2 attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
3 confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
4 activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
5 load_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
6 unload_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
7 detach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
8 attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
9 confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
10 activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
11 load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
12 unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
13 assemble_transport_leg origin_availability_alpha destination_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha destination_node_alpha transport_leg_alpha
14 execute_schedule_dispatch shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma dispatch_slot_alpha

Now we have 14 actions.

Could we reduce further? Perhaps we can avoid detaching task profile if we instead attach to origin first, prepare origin, then detach, then attach to destination? But final state requires origin task profile linked, destination not required. So we could attach to origin first, prepare origin, activate origin, load/unload origin, then detach, then attach to destination, prepare destination, activate destination, load/unload destination, and keep destination task profile linked? But goal does not require destination task profile linked, so we could keep it linked or detach; either fine. However we need to have origin task profile linked at end, so we need to keep it linked after we finish origin processing. If we attach to origin first, then after origin processing we could keep it linked (good). Then we need to prepare destination; we would need task profile for destination, but it's currently linked to origin, not available. So we would need to detach from origin first, then attach to destination, prepare destination, then reattach to origin? That would be more steps.

Thus current approach seems minimal.

Could we avoid loading/unloading for origin and destination by using other actions to get occupied/ready/confirmed/locked? Let's examine alternatives.

Goal requires origin_node_occupied and origin_node_ready. To get occupied we need load_origin_payload (or assemble_origin_loaded_leg? Actually assemble_origin_loaded_leg sets origin_leg_loaded but not node occupied). There's also assemble_fully_loaded_leg which sets origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded but not node occupied. Node occupied only comes from load_*_payload actions. So we need load payload to get node occupied.

Goal requires origin_node_ready; we can get that via activate_origin_node (sets ready) or via unload_origin_payload (sets ready). Actually unload_origin_payload sets origin_node_ready true. So we could possibly skip activate_origin_node and rely on unload to set ready? Let's see: unload_origin_payload precondition includes origin_node_occupied (true after load) and origin_availability_node_linked etc. Effect includes origin_node_ready true. So we could load then unload, and we would get origin_node_ready true from unload, and origin_node_occupied true from load (still true after unload? unload does not affect origin_node_occupied). So after load+unload we have origin_node_occupied true, origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_locked true (from load), origin_availability_confirmed true (from unload). That's exactly what we need for origin! So we can skip activate_origin_node action.

Similarly for destination: we can load then unload to get destination_node_occupied true (from load), destination_node_ready true (from unload), destination_availability_locked true (from load), destination_availability_confirmed true (from unload). So we can skip activate_destination_node as well.

Thus we can eliminate both activate actions.

Let's verify preconditions for load and unload.

Load origin payload requires: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha, origin_availability_node_linked, cargo_available, not origin_availability_locked.

We need candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (we will have after confirm). origin_availability_node_linked true. cargo_available initially true, but we will have used cargo for destination load earlier; after destination load/unload we will have cargo_available true again (since unload returns cargo). So we can do origin load after we have cargo available again.

Not origin_availability_locked: we need it false before load. Initially false; we haven't locked origin yet. Good.

Thus we can do origin load after we have cargo available.

Now unload origin payload requires: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_occupied, origin_payload_linked, not origin_availability_confirmed.

We will have candidate_prepared true, candidate_task_profile_linked true (we will attach), origin_availability_node_linked true, origin_node_occupied true (from load), origin_payload_linked true (from load), not origin_availability_confirmed true (init false). So unload works.

